title Caravan unhand -- a child is weighed by the line it holds, never by the ceiling its domain was granted
prompt Keaton set the loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, send each finished increment as its own signed round, and stop at the custody gates.
think Standfast first. Walked crux/REDS.md end to end: rows 81, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87 all carry closure notes, 85 reopened and closed on 20260819.134229, 84 closed on 20260819.145920. No open agent-closable red stands, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the newest three logs' recommend lines rather than from REMEMBER alone. Understudy's recommend named the next question exactly -- whether a run may hand a child in flight a new line, narrowing or widening the grants it already holds while it holds them.
think Read the arc before writing a line of it: understudy.rye whole, replace.rye's re-exports, intent.rye's narrow and its two readings, commute.rye's admissible and pair_contends. The reading that mattered came from intent.rye's own banner, which says plainly why it left the isolation room at the ceiling -- a channel joins two domains at every instant, and a bell may ring at any moment of a hop.
think Both reasons are true of the CHANNEL. Neither is true of the shared-memory refusal, which had simply never been revisited. So the honest rung is not reaching into a running child at all: it is spending the proof understudy already made. intent.narrow hands each child capabilities for the arcs it names this turn and drops the write bit wherever the item declared a read, and the child cannot reach past that line. A line handed over is a fact about the child, so a run may weigh it as one.
think Measurement said the existing corpus could not show the finding. Every declaration in caravan/systems pairs a written shared region with a channel, and the channel refusal dominates -- so the ceiling and the held line never disagree there. Authored serial_three_clients_board.bron for exactly the missing shape: client_a writes a board its siblings read, with no channel joining any client to any other. The menu declaration was authored for commute.rye the same way, so this follows the arc's own habit rather than inventing one.
think The two refusals fell out of the shape rather than being chosen. The ceiling reading needs only a domain name, which every live child already carries; the held reading needs the whole line, so the run must remember one per live child. UnhandUnheld is that memory, since a forgotten child is an unweighed one. UnhandWidened is the reach, since a remembered line claiming a write the document never granted would admit a newcomer the ceiling rightly blocks.
think The generalization test wanted a widest line, and the board declaration cannot carry one -- every client there reaches five regions against cycle.max_hops of four. Rather than weaken the test, ran it over the elder serial_three_clients.bron where each client reaches exactly three, and named that bound in the module rather than leaving a reader to wonder.
obs The honest trade is printed rather than hidden: the narrower room costs MORE to read. 48 tests at the door by the held line against 36 by the ceiling, both derived from the bounds themselves. A run pays a few more tests and buys room for work that never touches, and the comptime assert states that direction positively.
obs The lap measured a real win on metal rather than a claimed one. One plan run twice reaps 7 children and carries 1 home either way, with 2 at once by the ceiling against 3 by the lines held, and 8 slots left unspent against 1.
obs All four RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN was claimed. Dropping the memory refusal panics at index out of bounds: index 0, len 0 -- a forgotten child shown as a crash rather than argued about. Dropping the reach refusal weighs a line claiming an ungranted write. Dropping the channel refusal admits a domain joined by a channel beside its peer. Answering the door by the ceiling in both runs shows the finding as a failure: the narrower room bought no room at all, 2 against 2.
obs Docs stayed synced in the same round. Understudy's README limit line and its witness header both said the new-line question belonged to the vision room until a witness binds it, and a witness now binds it, so both point at the rung below instead.
obs A ratchet worth naming and not opening this round: the caravan family has 48 per-rung witnesses and no loom that hears them all, while the crypto family grew one after REDS #81. Nothing fired unheard here, so this is a ratchet rather than a red -- a candidate keystone for its own lap.
obs The limit is named plainly rather than left for a reader to find: a run weighs a child by the line it was handed at spawn, and that line never moves while the child runs. Whether a child may give back an arc it has finished with -- a line shrinking mid-flight, so the door widens the moment the work narrows -- is the next rung's question.
loom witness=caravan_unhand_witness wall_ms=1364 rings=41 door_tests_held=48 door_tests_ceiling=36
loom caravan=unhand_lap children=7 homed=1 peak_ceiling=2 peak_held=3 slots_unspent_ceiling=8 slots_unspent_held=1 widest_pairs=9
file caravan/unhand.rye the rung -- two rooms at the door, two refusals earned, a supervisor that remembers one line per live child
file caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron the declaration the finding needed -- a board one client writes and its siblings read, with no channel joining them
file tools/caravan_unhand_witness.rish the witness -- GREEN on metal, every claim read natively rather than through a shell quote
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, and understudy's limit line repointed at the rung that answers it
file tools/caravan_understudy_witness.rish its limit header repointed, since the question it deferred now has a witness
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge refreshed to this rung, the prior edge condensed to a pointer
recommend keep-going the next rung's question is already named -- whether a child may give back an arc it has finished with, so a line shrinks mid-flight and the door widens the moment the work narrows. Mechanical, single-module, and the arc's own habit answers how to shape it. The caravan witness loom stands beside it as an equally honest keystone.
